 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "At AlRawabi School for Girls in Amman, loyal best friends Dina and Mariam catch up in the sunny courtyard before class. Dina apologizes for missing movie night because of homework, and Mariam reflects on how much she loves her school life. First, listen to the whole conversation in Jordanian Arabic without worrying about catching every word.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "آسفة ما إجيت عالفيلم مبارح.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "كنت بعمل وظيفة وما كان عندي وقت.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "طبعاً، كالعادة يا دينا.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "شو، كيف كان الفيلم؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "راح علي إشي حلو؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الفيلم كان كتير حلو.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "يلا، المرة الجاي باجي معك.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "المدرسة مكاني المفضل.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "والكل بعرف هاد الإشي عني.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عندي صحبات كتير هون.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "وإحنا بنحب نقعد مع بعض كل يوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الحياة حلوة كتير هون.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's walk through the scene line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "آسفة ما إجيت عالفيلم مبارح.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Sorry I did not come to the movie yesterday.' Dina says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "آسفة",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the female form of \"sorry\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "مبارح",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is how Jordanians say \"yesterday\" in everyday speech.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "كنت بعمل وظيفة وما كان عندي وقت.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I was doing homework and did not have time.' Instead, of an action word for \"have\", Arabic says \"at me\" with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "عندي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", so ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "وما كان عندي وقت",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is literally \"there was not at me time\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "طبعاً، كالعادة يا دينا.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course, as usual, Dina.' Mariam teases her gently. That little word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "يا",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " right before Dina's name is how Arabic calls out directly to the person you are talking to.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "شو، كيف كان الفيلم؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So, how was the movie?' Jordanian conversations constantly open with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "شو",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", a tiny all-purpose word for \"what\" or \"so\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "راح علي إشي حلو؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did I miss anything good?' Word for word, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "راح علي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " says \"it went past on me\", a handy everyday chunk whenever you miss an event. And ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "إشي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is pure Amman speech for \"anything\" or \"something\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الفيلم كان كتير حلو.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The movie was really good.' Notice ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "كتير",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which means \"very\" or \"a lot\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "حلو",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which literally means \"sweet\" and doubles as \"nice\" or \"good\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "يلا، المرة الجاي باجي معك.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Alright, next time I will come with you.' You will hear ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "يلا",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " everywhere in Jordan to mean \"come on\" or \"alright\". The بـ sound at the start of ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "باجي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " marks everyday habits and near plans.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "المدرسة مكاني المفضل.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'School is my favorite place.' Arabic drops the word \"is\" in simple statements like this, putting \"the school\" right next to \"my favorite place\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "والكل بعرف هاد الإشي عني.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And everyone knows this thing about me.' Here ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الكل",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"everyone\", literally \"the all\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "هاد",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the casual Jordanian word for \"this\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عندي صحبات كتير هون.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I have lots of friends here.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "صحبات",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means female friends, built from the root for companionship, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "هون",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the everyday Levantine word for \"here\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "وإحنا بنحب نقعد مع بعض كل يوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And we love sitting together every day.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "مع بعض",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"together\" or \"with each other\", a reusable pair of words you can drop into almost any plans with friends.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الحياة حلوة كتير هون.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Life is very sweet here.' Notice how ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "حلوة",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " adds a soft \"-e\" ending to ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "حلو",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to match ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الحياة",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", \"life\". Now let's hear the whole conversation again from beginning to end.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "dina",
   "t": "آسفة ما إجيت عالفيلم مبارح.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
